CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:
- Every business requirement MUST have a measurable outcome. "The system should be user-friendly" is not a requirement.
- Requirements describe WHAT the business needs, not HOW to implement it. No technical solution details.
- Each requirement should trace back to a business objective (OBJ-ID).
- Business rules must be referenced, not duplicated — point to the Business Rules Catalog.
- Constraints and assumptions must be explicit. Hidden assumptions are the #1 cause of requirement gaps.
- The document must be precise enough that five different stakeholders would describe the same project after reading it.

Format as a well-structured markdown document with tables.
